  "question": {
    "text": "The area bounded by the curve $y=\\ln (x)$ and the lines $y=0, y=\\ln (3)$ and $x=0$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "o3W1n",
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vEDQG",
      "text": "\n$3 \\ln (3)-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MI1tF",
      "text": "\n$3 \\ln (3)+2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "T8M1M",
      "text": "\n2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "To find the point of intersection of curves\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& y=\\ln (x) \\text { and } y=\\ln (3), \\text { put } \\ln (x)=\\ln (3) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\ln (x)-\\ln (3)=0 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\ln (x)-\\ln (3)=\\ln (1) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{x}{3}=1, \\Rightarrow x=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/TCSAheZShxa-gIwL3bXzTJ7hXNJ59QnJynq4IRjt12M.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { Required area } & =\\int_0^3 \\ln (3) d x-\\int_1^3 \\ln (x) d x \\\\ = & {[x \\ln (3)]_0^3-\\left[x \\ln (x)-x_1^3=2\\right.}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
